{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778596396280,"sessionID":"ses_1e365ad2bffe5HRu2su8GtgBuO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-93a1fa7838844988","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json"},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"Please check that the term does not already exist by using the ontology search tool OLS:\\nhttps://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl\\n\\n\\n**Preferred term label**\\nUnclassified Fallopian Tube Progenitor (UCFP)\\n\\n**Synonyms** (add reference(s), please)\\nPrior work (PMID: 35320732) has referred to similar UCFP cells as clusters 2-1 and 2-2 that can give rise to epithelial and endothelial/stromal cell types through scRNA-seq and trajectory inference.\\n\\n**Definition** (free text, with reference(s), please. PubMed ID format is PMID:XXXXXX)\\nWe propose a new, broad definition for the observed \\\"dual-feature\\\" human fallopian tube progenitor-like cells that simultaneously express epithelial (e.g., EpCAM/CD326) and endothelial (e.g., PECAM1/CD31) markers, both on the cell surface and by RNA expression that can give rise to ciliated and secretory cell types, and potentially to endothelial/stromal cell types. These \\\"dual-feature\\\" unclassified fallopian tube progenitor cells have primary been observed by single-cell RNA-seq (scRNA-seq), flow cytometry, and immunofluorescence, with the UCFP term proposed in PMID: 40475517.\\n\\n**Parent cell type term** (check the hierarchy here https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl)\\nI am not entirely sure as these could exist under CL:4052019 or CL:4052018. \\n\\n**Anatomical structure where the cell type is found** (check Uberon for anatomical structures: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/uberon)\\nHuman fallopian tube\\n\\n**Your ORCID**\\n0000-0002-1482-1032\\n\\n**Additional notes or concerns**\\nI'm sure this is incomplete and is my first attempt at this :) Thank you and my apologies in advance!\\n\\n\",\n3:   \"comments\": [\n4:     {\n5:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-863P-Pz\",\n6:       \"author\": {\n7:         \"login\": \"dosumis\"\n8:       },\n9:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n10:       \"body\": \"Looks good, but would prefer something like 'dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell' as a name. I guess 'unclassified' is historical at this point - you just classified it.\",\n11:       \"createdAt\": \"2025-07-15T16:55:22Z\",\n12:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": true,\n13:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n14:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n15:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n16:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3196#issuecomment-3074417651\",\n17:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n18:     },\n19:     {\n20:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-8680l9V\",\n21:       \"author\": {\n22:         \"login\": \"Caroline-99\"\n23:       },\n24:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n25:       \"body\": \"Discussion with Ben: He is happy with us using `dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell` as the main label in CL.\",\n26:       \"createdAt\": \"2025-08-08T13:26:04Z\",\n27:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n28:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n29:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n30:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n31:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3196#issuecomment-3167903573\",\n32:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n33:     },\n34:     {\n35:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-869i1dc\",\n36:       \"author\": {\n37:         \"login\": \"Caroline-99\"\n38:       },\n39:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n40:       \"body\": \"**Updates on text and logical defs (have been reviewed by @biobenkj ):**\\n\\n**label**\\ndual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell\\n\\n**textual definition**\\n\\nA bipotent progenitor cell within the human fallopian tube epithelium, characterized by the concurrent expression of epithelial (e.g., EpCAM/CD326) and endothelial (e.g., PECAM1/CD31) markers at both the cell surface and transcript levels. This cell has the capacity to differentiate into ciliated and secretory epithelial cells, as well as potentially endothelial/stromal lineages. Positioned at the apex of lineage bifurcation, the cell exhibits stem-like and endothelial features, representing an intermediate developmental state between undifferentiated progenitors and lineage-committed epithelial cells.\\n\\n PMID: [40475517](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40475517/)\\n\\n**Synonyms**\\n\\nnon-ciliated secretory epithelial cell 2-1 (NCSE2-1 cells) - related synonym -  PMID: [35320732](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35320732/)\\nnon-ciliated secretory epithelial cell 2-2 (NCSE2-2 cells) - related synonym -  PMID: [35320732](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35320732/)\\nunclassified fallopian tube progenitors - exact-  PMID: [40475517](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40475517/)\\n\\n**Logical definition:**\\n\\n'progenitor cell'\\n'part of' some 'fallopian tube epithelium'\\n'in taxon' some 'Homo sapiens'\\n'develops into' some 'fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell'\\n'develops into' some 'fallopian tube multiciliated epithelial cell'\\n\",\n41:       \"createdAt\": \"2025-08-12T16:02:12Z\",\n42:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": true,\n43:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n44:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n45:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n46:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3196#issuecomment-3180025692\",\n47:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n48:     }\n49:   ],\n50:   \"title\": \"[NTR] Unclassified Fallopian Tube Progenitor (UCFP)\",\n51:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3196\"\n52: }\n\n(End of file - total 52 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"Please check that the term does not already exist by using the ontology search tool OLS:\\nhttps://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl\\n\\n\\n**Preferred term label**\\nUnclassified Fallopian Tube Progenitor (UCFP)\\n\\n**Synonyms** (add reference(s), please)\\nPrior work (PMID: 35320732) has referred to similar UCFP cells as clusters 2-1 and 2-2 that can give rise to epithelial and endothelial/stromal cell types through scRNA-seq and trajectory inference.\\n\\n**Definition** (free text, with reference(s), please. PubMed ID format is PMID:XXXXXX)\\nWe propose a new, broad definition for the observed \\\"dual-feature\\\" human fallopian tube progenitor-like cells that simultaneously express epithelial (e.g., EpCAM/CD326) and endothelial (e.g., PECAM1/CD31) markers, both on the cell surface and by RNA expression that can give rise to ciliated and secretory cell types, and potentially to endothelial/stromal cell types. These \\\"dual-feature\\\" unclassified fallopian tube progenitor cells have primary been observed by single-cell RNA-seq (scRNA-seq), flow cytometry, and immunofluorescence, with the UCFP term proposed in PMID: 40475517.\\n\\n**Parent cell type term** (check the hierarchy here https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl)\\nI am not entirely sure as these could exist under CL:4052019 or CL:4052018. \\n\\n**Anatomical structure where the cell type is found** (check Uberon for anatomical structures: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/uberon)\\nHuman fallopian tube\\n\\n**Your ORCID**\\n0000-0002-1482-1032\\n\\n**Additional notes or concerns**\\nI'm sure this is incomplete and is my first attempt at this :) Thank you and my apologies in advance!\\n\\n\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-863P-Pz\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"dosumis\"\n      },\n      \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n      \"body\": \"Looks good, but would prefer something like 'dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell' as a name. I guess 'unclassified' is historical at this point - you just classified it.\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2025-07-15